    "name": "Napa Cabbage",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Young Napa cabbage, also known as Baby Napa cabbage or&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=a2e43e9e1c69768b&amp;rlz=1CAVNCX_enUS1049US1049&amp;sxsrf=AE3TifOO2Ory36ukNLTr2e1Qy0IaOT4nKA%3A1748377088378&amp;q=Wawa+Choy&amp;sa=X&amp;sqi=2&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjp6aSavMSNAxXHAjQIHW-eIEIQxccNegQIJxAB&amp;mstk=AUtExfD0m135dxLhfeuOYYag2-5g4GA_LKme3au1rFP87MXvI32thnwxPJM_Z0HVQq_-aN0SYdf4Q9wIwDO1B3SjQZBgkJlJHUUoP6IltEaKhhqvDFR1-bCX8y05DTlalEN2uqWOOo3N5-qnIJmJnVgy65Iedpl2Q9Z3mTlwY_lrHeTA9ov_8s0ybUQp8fi6RDRquTWWKxz957Il7AibGGLcx6KOdGAk7l1-ps0Lma2yQop4aK8NPnNCDjdP_ZjGxxtzjYJYjXcq6gv9GNq-L9f3JiyM&amp;csui=3\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Wawa Choy</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">,&nbsp;is&nbsp;a tender, sweeter version of regular Napa cabbage.&nbsp;It's harvested earlier, resulting in softer, more delicate leaves and a milder flavor.&nbsp;While both can be used interchangeably in many recipes, Baby Napa cabbage is often preferred for its delicate texture and milder taste.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Weight is 1 to 2 lbs.</span></p>",
